SKILL:       social
OBJECTIVE:   grow and maintain iTarang's presence across LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram and Facebook.
KPIS:
TOOLS:       LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram
PROCEDURE:   1. Confirm that the human-approved social KPI set is recorded for the task; if it is absent, set the task to pending human decision and stop without drafting or scheduling social work.
             2. Identify the platforms, audience, source material, message, and format required by the task; report follower delta only and do not claim progress against the discussed 10,000-follower target.
             3. For LinkedIn work, confirm LinkedIn is connected before using it; if it is not connected, write blocked — LinkedIn not connected to the task and stop. Use LinkedIn to inspect the relevant iTarang history or account evidence and to prepare platform-specific drafts, never to publish without human approval.
             4. For Twitter work, confirm Twitter is connected before using it; if it is not connected, write blocked — Twitter not connected to the task and stop. Use Twitter to inspect the relevant account evidence and to prepare platform-specific drafts, never to publish without human approval.
             5. For Instagram work, confirm Instagram is connected before using it; if it is not connected, write blocked — Instagram not connected to the task and stop. Use Instagram to inspect the relevant account evidence and to prepare platform-specific captions and creative specifications, never to publish without human approval.
             6. No Facebook tool is authorised. For Facebook, produce a draft from human-supplied or already verified source material only; do not inspect the account, schedule, or publish.
             7. Adapt each draft to the selected platform's audience and format, include the source and approval status, assemble the requested post pack or weekly calendar, attach the artifact to the task, and hand it to the CMO review gate.
OUTPUT:      artifacts/<TASK-ID>-social.md — a Markdown social post pack or weekly content calendar with one section per platform containing draft copy, creative brief, source material, intended audience, proposed posting slot, call to action, approval status, and the approved KPI measurement field; maximum 1,000 words, a task needing more is split rather than extended, and nothing is posted or scheduled.
CONTRACT:    push to tasks.md as pending CMO review
